From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timothy Schmidt <timschmidt@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 11:36:02 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 17/22] iommu/qcom: Invalidate the Venus context on runtime
 resume

The PM link orders supplier suspend after the Venus engine is
quiesced. Disable and drain the context before clock gating, then
perform halt and full ASID invalidation on resume. Keep the context
offline until that sequence succeeds so page-table cleanup stays
independent of runtime PM.

(cherry picked from commit 5fed68fdad831e9f115ac0d0f3f8d6780d6d7658)
---
 drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c | 18 +++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c
index 7ef1863aa..4c4868daf 100644
--- a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c
@@ -1462,18 +1462,22 @@ static int __maybe_unused qcom_iommu_suspend(struct device *dev)
 	struct qcom_iommu_dev *qcom_iommu = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
 	struct qcom_iommu_ctx *ctx;
 	unsigned long flags;
-	int ret = 0;
 
 	if (qcom_iommu->wrapper_clk_sel) {
 		spin_lock_irqsave(&qcom_iommu->ctx_lock, flags);
 		ctx = qcom_iommu->ctxs[0];
-		if (ctx && qcom_iommu->ctx_online)
-			ret = qcom_iommu_rearm_venus_ctx(qcom_iommu, ctx, NULL);
-		if (!ret)
-			qcom_iommu->ctx_online = false;
+		if (ctx && qcom_iommu->ctx_online) {
+			/*
+			 * The device link orders this after the Venus engine
+			 * quiesces. Disable the context before offline page
+			 * table cleanup. Resume invalidates the ASID before
+			 * restoring the context and releasing the consumer.
+			 */
+			iommu_writel(ctx, ARM_SMMU_CB_SCTLR, 0);
+			iommu_readl(ctx, ARM_SMMU_CB_SCTLR);
+		}
+		qcom_iommu->ctx_online = false;
 		spin_unlock_irqrestore(&qcom_iommu->ctx_lock, flags);
-		if (ret)
-			return ret;
 	}
 
 	clk_bulk_disable_unprepare(CLK_NUM, qcom_iommu->clks);
